WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.500
What’s up, my well read ballas?

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.780
This week, we takin’ things to the MAX wit
Where the Wild Things Are, by Maurice Sendak.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.880
It’s gettin’ hella late up at da crib,
and instead of catchin some z’s, lil shawty

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.940
Max sportin some fly-ass wolf threadz and
hoppin’ round like a bunny on bath salts.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:40.530
We see him pitchin’ tents, chasin’ a dog
wit a FORK, and just makin’ a damn mess.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:45.710
Instead of callin’ the exorcist, Max’s
mama all like “CHILL you WILD THANG.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:50.960
Matta’ fact, you betta hustle yo crazy ass
up to bed, cuz you ain’t gettin NO DINNER

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:51.960
tonight!”

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:52.960
DAMN GIRL!

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.890
A growin boy need his grub.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:01:01.470
Max roll up to his room pissed as hell when
“OH SHIT!”- a buncha TREES start growin’

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.739
in his room and a damn OCEAN tumbles by.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:09.179
Sounds like this lil dude been growin a diff
kind of tree, naw mean?

00:01:09.179 --> 00:01:15.420
So boy hop up on a fly-ass boat and start
flowin down da ocean fo’ nearly a YEAR.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:20.100
Finally Max land in this funked-out spot where
a bunch of busted-ass beasts called “WILD

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.539
THANGS” be chillin.

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:26.409
When deez big headed b*tches see Max, they
WIG OUT and try to make him all scurred.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:29.639
Man, this s**t like Sesame Street on a bad
trip!

00:01:29.639 --> 00:01:32.740
But Max is a hard-ass gangsta who don’t
back down.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.479
He start mad doggin em’ and hollas out "CHILL,
b*tches!"

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:37.479
And BOOM!

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:41.500
They all put da hustle aside and slow their
roll!

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.500
DAYUM!

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.860
This lil’ playa got some big boy balls, don't he!

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:51.099
Afta’ seein how real Max be, dem muppet-lookin
mofos give him a phat crown and make him king

00:01:51.099 --> 00:01:52.579
of all wild thangz.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:56.660
To celebrate his balla status, Max throws a
BANGIN’ rumpus!"

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:57.940
Aww yeah!

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:58.940
PAR-TAY!

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:03.920
Max and his crew are ragin’ under the moon
when outta nowhere, Max hollas “Stop!”

00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:07.859
and sends dem bustas to bed with NO SUPPER”.

00:02:07.859 --> 00:02:12.970
Even though he rockin the crown like a G now,
this lil’ bruh start feelin’ mad lonely.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:16.860
He jus’ wanna be at the spot where someone
love him da most.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.760
Basically- he miss his mama!

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.880
Max gets the munchies and decide to head home,
but the wild thangs all like: "Don’t leave

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.280
us, playa!"

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:29.140
But Max be all: "Too late!" and throws up
the deuce.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:33.800
Back at da crib, Max finds his hot dinner
still on da table jus’ waitin’ for him

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.189
to get his grub on.

00:02:35.189 --> 00:02:37.380
Sounds like soul food to me!

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:41.020
Mmm-mmm-MMM! I love you Momma!

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.400
When it comes to the children's lit game,
this book right here broke all kinda rules.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:55.860
See, most kids books reppin childhood as just
sippin on juiceboxes and playing a little grabass.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:01.040
But this book right here explore da dark shit
dat go down inside the minds of lil kids.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:06.620
Cuz on da real, it ain’t always all good
when you a kid- you gotta deal wit some real raw

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.620
emotions.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.790
Dat faraway land of wild thangz represents
da psychology of a young blood dealin with

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.680
a booty-load of mixed up emotions.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:21.010
This hood serve as a spot where Max can recognize
all his confusion and anger, work through

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.260
it, and understand what’s REALLY important
in his life.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.489
At first, Max all geeked to chill with the
wild thangz.

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:32.530
Cuz wit dem, he can live out his beastly side
without havin’ his hater-ass mama always

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:33.530
tryna’ control him.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.950
But when he gettin crunk up at da rumpus,
he recognize dat even gettin lit ain’t gonna

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:38.950
make him happy.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:44.260
So when he kills da party by screamin, “now
stop,” he show dat he got mo’ control

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:45.480
over his anger.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.230
You can almost hear his balls drop.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.420
And at the end of the story, lil’ Max recognize
dat his mama ain’t controllin’ him just

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.090
to be a b*tch.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:55.090
Nah, blood.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.969
She just really cares about him.

00:03:56.969 --> 00:04:02.150
Dat hot grub at da end reppin da fact that
no matta’ how much he actin’ like a shit,

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:05.150
he’ll always have da unconditional love
of his mama.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:08.540
Look, da world is a messed up place, even
fo’ children.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:13.500
But instead of just sweepin it under the rug,
kids can use their imagination to beast through

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.049
all dat loneliness and isolation.

00:04:16.049 --> 00:04:20.810
Like Sendak say: “[There are] games children
must conjure up to combat an awful fact of

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:26.820
childhood: the fact of their vulnerability
to fear, anger, hate, frustration — all

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.850
the emotions.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:33.310
... Through fantasy, Max, the hero of my book,
discharges his anger against his mother, and

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:37.440
returns to the real world sleepy, hungry,
and at peace with himself.”

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.800
Yo, thanks for kickin it wit your boy, man! Peace!

